 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Pop the seat post out, and measure it from top of the seat tube. That's the height range for seat post. You should be just above middle of the area marked on the seat tube. Going too far forward puts your weight on the seat bolt threads. Going too far forward puts all your weight on the seat bolt threads, and you'll wearing them out. Then lengthen it, or try a bike with a taller seat tube. Then this isn't the bike for you. Look at mountain bikes with wide handlebars instead. They' much more comfortable. You' lose some speed, but road bikes are much faster than mountain bikes on flat terrain. Which do you like doing more? Zigzagging up hills, or flying along flat roads?",
